invariant reading
1. This is the AP-tail analogue of FKN/root-packet structure: the
   relevant perturbation is the addressed packet (holes, tails, carry,
   mouth survival), not the number of replacements.
2. The proof target is a mouth-damage theorem: once a packet damages the
   four drop-6 mouths or opens genuinely new odd-shell carry, it should
   pay the AP-second threshold before scalar measure is used.
3. Any below-threshold packet retained here should be treated as a finite
   root-packet template feeding HYP-2654/HYP-2659/HYP-2660, while the
   pruned tail side routes to HYP-2655/HYP-2658.

